      <figure class="art-gallery-card art-gallery-card--salmon" tabindex="0"><img src="{{ '/assets/art/salmon-study.jpg' | url }}" alt="Illustration of a salmon leaping beside a waterfall" loading="lazy"><figcaption><span>Upstream</span></figcaption></figure>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="art-series art-series--colour">
  <div class="art-shell">
    <header class="art-series-heading"><div><p class="art-index">03</p><h2>Colour and atmosphere</h2></div><p>I like acrylic markers because they are quicker to reach for than paint, but a mistake cannot simply be erased. They make me work in layers, keep an eye on both the whole and the detail, and be bolder with colour. For me, they sit somewhere between drawing, painting and digital work, only without an Undo button.</p></header>
    <div class="art-gallery-row art-gallery-row--three" aria-label="Colour and atmosphere">
